# Tracking Server - S2S Attribution for XM Partners

## Overview
This is a production-ready Node.js tracking server that handles:
- Click ID registration from landing pages
- Telegram user mapping
- XM Partner postback conversions
- Real-time dashboard data

## Installation

### 1. Install Dependencies
```bash
npm install
```

### 2. Configure Environment
Copy `.env` file and update with your values:
```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Update these values:
- `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` — from @BotFather
- `TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_ID` — your channel ID
- `META_PIXEL_ID` — your Meta pixel (if using CAPI)
- `META_CAPI_TOKEN` — your Meta CAPI token

### 3. Start Server
```bash
npm start
```

Server will start on `http://localhost:3000` and automatically:
- Create `tracking.db` SQLite database
- Create all required tables (clicks, conversions, telegram_users, etc.)
- Log initialization status

## API Endpoints

### Health Check
```
GET /
Response: { "status": "ok", "database": "connected" }
```

### Register Click (from Landing Page)
```
POST /api/click
Body: {
  "click_id": "abc12345",
  "fbclid": "IwAR2...",
  "fbp": "fb.1...",
  "utm_source": "facebook",
  "utm_campaign": "campaign_1"
}
Response: { "status": "ok", "click_id": "abc12345" }
```

### Map Telegram User
```
POST /api/telegram-map
Body: {
  "telegram_id": "123456789",
  "click_id": "abc12345",
  "telegram_username": "@username"
}
Response: { "status": "ok", "message": "Telegram user mapped" }
```

### XM Postback (Conversion)
```
GET /postback?click_id={tag}&amount={deposit_amount}&event={status}
Response: OK (HTTP 200)
```

### Test Postback
```
GET /test-postback?click_id=TEST123&amount=500&event=FTD
Response: { "click_id_found": true, "conversions_count": 1, "status": "test_ok" }
```

### Dashboard Data
```
GET /dashboard-data
Response: { "summary": {...}, "conversions": [...] }
```

### Debug Logs
```
GET /logs
Response: { "logs": [...] }
```

### Statistics
```
GET /stats
Response: { "clicks": 100, "conversions": 25, ... }
```

## Database

The database is automatically created with these tables:

- **clicks** — User clicks from landing page (fbclid, UTMs, etc.)
- **telegram_users** — Maps Telegram ID to click ID
- **conversions** — XM deposit events
- **postback_logs** — Audit trail of all postbacks
- **meta_capi_events** — Future Meta CAPI integration

## Testing Workflow

### 1. Test Server is Running
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/
# Should return: { "status": "ok", ... }
```

### 2. Register a Click
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/click \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "click_id": "test_123",
    "fbclid": "test_fbclid",
    "utm_source": "facebook"
  }'
```

### 3. Test Postback
```bash
curl "http://localhost:3000/test-postback?click_id=test_123&amount=500&event=FTD"
```

### 4. View Dashboard Data
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/dashboard-data
```

### 5. View Logs
```bash
curl http://localhost:3000/logs
```

## Deployment to Hostinger

1. Push code to GitHub repository
2. In Hostinger Node.js section:
   - Connect GitHub repo
   - Set startup file: `server.js`
   - Set domain: `track.app.dilpreetbrar.com`
   - Deploy

3. After deployment, set environment variables in Hostinger:
   - `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN`
   - `TELEGRAM_CHANNEL_ID`
   - Other `.env` variables

4. Restart application

## Troubleshooting

### "better-sqlite3" build error
Solution: Ensure Node.js version is 18+ and build tools are available
```bash
npm install --build-from-source
```

### Database locked error
- Usually temporary
- Server will auto-retry
- Can safely restart

### CORS errors
Add your domain to `CORS_ORIGINS` in `.env`

### Click not found on postback
1. Verify click was registered (check `/dashboard-data`)
2. Check exact click_id spelling
3. View `/logs` for postback audit trail

## Production Checklist

- [ ] `.env` file configured with real values
- [ ] `.env` file NOT committed to GitHub
- [ ] `package.json` dependencies installed
- [ ] Server tested locally: `npm start`
- [ ] All endpoints tested with curl/Postman
- [ ] Deployed to Hostinger
- [ ] Domain verified: `https://track.app.dilpreetbrar.com/`
- [ ] XM postback URL configured
- [ ] Telegram bot added as admin to channel
- [ ] Landing page script updated with correct API URL

## Architecture

```
Landing Page (fbclid, UTMs) 
    ↓ POST /api/click
    → Database: clicks table
    ↓
Telegram Bot (click_id)
    ↓ POST /api/telegram-map
    → Database: telegram_users table
    ↓
XM Partners (deposit)
    ↓ GET /postback?click_id=X&amount=Y
    → Database: conversions table
    ↓
Dashboard (read /dashboard-data)
    → Analytics & ROI calculations
```

## Support

For issues:
1. Check `/logs` endpoint
2. Check server console output
3. Verify database file exists: `tracking.db`
4. Ensure all dependencies installed: `npm install`